    {
      "turn": 3,
      "doctor_question": "How long have you been hearing these voices?",
      "targeted_symptom": "psychotic_symptoms_duration",
      "patient_response": "Um, the voices from the walls and my phone... it's been about three months now. Right around the end of the second quarter. Which is always just an incredibly stressful time anyway because of the quarterly reviews. We had this massive catered lunch for the partners that week, and the catering company completely messed up the order. I specifically requested an assortment of gluten-free options because two of our main investors insist they have Celiac disease. Though, honestly, you never know these days if it's a real medical issue or just a fad diet. Everyone wants to be gluten-free or keto now. \n\nI actually tried keto for about a week last year, and I just felt so incredibly sluggish the whole time. You really don't realize how much you miss bread until you absolutely cannot have it. There's this little artisan bakery down the street from my condo that makes the most incredible sourdough. The crust is just perfectly crispy, and they bake it fresh every single morning. If I'm out on my balcony early enough, and the wind is blowing the right direction, I can smell it baking. The owner is this older gentleman, always has flour dusted all over his apron, and he sweeps the sidewalk out front at exactly 6:00 AM every day. He has this very rhythmic way of sweeping, just back and forth, back and forth... \n\nWait, I'm sorry, I lost my train of thought completely. What were we just talking about? Did you need to know something else about the bakery?",
